# Managed by home/srvs/oracle-skills.nix; edits here are overwritten.
#
# A skill is a STORE with unattended writers, not a document somebody owns:
# chatter itself writes one with `make_skill`, on either machine, and an
# unresolved conflict here does not merely flag that file — it aborts the tick
# and stops the whole base syncing in either direction until someone notices.
# So every markdown file gets the same policy the boards get: the real 3-way
# merge FIRST (so two edits to different sections both survive), and only a
# genuine collision falls back to the more recent side, whole. Symmetric —
# neither host is privileged. Losing sides stay reachable in history.
#
# Requires merge.recentwins.driver, which oracle-skills-setup.sh registers on
# every tick. Without that registration these lines are INERT and git falls
# back to the default merge — i.e. back to the wedged sync.
*.md merge=recentwins

# Tool manifests (tools/*.json) are written by the same unattended hands and
# would wedge the sync the same way. Same policy, and the union fallback at the
# bottom of the driver — which would emit invalid JSON — is only reachable when
# neither side can be dated, i.e. never on this timer.
*.json merge=recentwins
